Recorded games for tools/compare-baseline ("make test").

Each directory holds the settings files the game is started with
(TRIPLANE_HOME), the recorded controls (record.dta), the random seed
(record.ran), the random numbers seen while recording (record.000) and
the command line for playback (args).

The games were recorded with an older version, and the gameplay has
changed since. During playback the game therefore reports "Random
failure" from the start and the planes do not fly the recorded game.
The replays are still deterministic, which is all the baseline
comparison needs.

To record a new game, use a fresh directory as TRIPLANE_HOME:

TRIPLANE_HOME=triplane-testsuite/NAME build/triplane -record -autostart -solomenumission 0 -autoquit -nofullscreen

Leave out "-solomenumission 0" for a multiplayer game. Then write the
playback command line to triplane-testsuite/NAME/args:

-playback -autostart -solomenumission 0 -autoquit -speed -debugtrace -nofullscreen

The *-vga directories are copies of the recordings with svga=0 in
triplane.cfg, so that the 320x200 drawing code is covered as well. All
original recordings were made in 800x600 mode.
